			"notes": "# Sink your friends' boats!\nSink your friends' boats is a primarily _server-side_ mod that allows for exactly one function: sink your friends' boats.\n\nThis mod also works on singleplayer and LAN worlds - only the host/server has to have the mod installed. It works the same as on the server.\n\nTo troll your friends, you HAVE to be a server operator (_/op_)\n\n## How do I sink them BOATS?\nIf you are a server operator (permission level 2) you gain access to the command\n\n```\n/sinkingboats\n```\nThis command gives you **5** options:\n### Add\n\n```\n/sinkingboats add <target>\n```\nThis command allows you to add a Player to the list of players whose boats will sink on water. It lets you autofill with Players that are online\n### Remove\n\n```\n/sinkingboats remove <target> \n```\nThis command allows you to remove a Player from the list of players whose boats will sink on water. It lets you autofill with Players that are online\n\n### clear\n\n```\n/sinkingboats clear\n```\nThis command clears the list. All players are free to endugle in travel by boat.\n### refresh\n\n```\n/sinkingboats refresh\n```\nThis is a \"just-in-case\" command which allows you to refresh the loaded list of players whose boats are to sink. This may be useful if you change the config file manually\n### list\n\n```\n/sinkingboats list\n```\nThis command allows operators to list all players whose boats will sink.\n\n## Manual manipulation\nIf you want to add players wihtout commands, you will find the config file under \n```\n/saves/[your_world]/boatsinking/boat-sinking-players.json\n```\nfor singleplayer and \n```\n/world/boatsinking/boat-sinking-players.json\n```\non servers. <br>\nTo add your own players, add their UUIDs to the json list."
		}
